    {
      "evidence": "template/scripts/worker_preflight.py, check_provider_credential: `if len(problems) == len(ctx.providers): raise PreflightRefusal(...)`. main() builds `providers` from `[*review_names, *filter(None, (args.provider, args.repair_provider))]`, which merges review and repair providers into one any-of check. A repair worker with a usable review provider and a broken `--repair-provider` credential therefore passes preflight. The failure then surfaces after claim, where only the review path (pr_review_gate.execute_review) converts CredentialError into a registered EnvironmentFailure. This cuts against the proposal's aim of stopping persistent environment defects before claim.",
      "id": "provider-credential-any-of-passes-repair",
      "severity": "advisory",
      "summary": "The provider-credential preflight condition passes when at least one named provider has a credential. A repair provider with no credential is not caught before claim if a review provider is usable."
